# Frozen list of ACCEPTED gitleaks findings for the Portal secret-scan ratchet.
#
# Each non-comment line is a gitleaks fingerprint (file:rule:line-ish) for a
# finding that has been reviewed and judged NOT a real secret — a test dummy,
# an example token, a public content hash the allowlist globs missed, etc.
# gitleaks excludes these on scan, so only NEW, un-fingerprinted findings fail.
#
# This is the exact analog of .swiftlint-baseline: it records pre-accepted
# noise only. scripts/check-secret-baseline-growth.py fails a PR that ADDS a
# fingerprint here (you'd be silently accepting a new finding instead of
# removing the secret). Adding a line is allowed ONLY with an explicit reason
# in the PR description — never to quietly wave a real credential through.
#
# The tree is currently CLEAN: zero findings, zero accepted fingerprints. Keep
# it that way. To add a genuine false-positive, paste the fingerprint gitleaks
# printed, one per line, with a trailing `# why it's safe` comment.
